{"name":"Coquelicot","hex":"#ff3800","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"coquelicot","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A reddish-orange colour; poppy."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a reddish-orange poppy colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coquelicot"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coquelicot","blocks":[{"text":"Coquelicot is a shade of red. The term is originally the French name for the wild corn poppy, Papaver rhoeas, which is distinguished by its bright red color and orange tint. It eventually passed into English usage as the name of a color based upon that of the flower. The first recorded use of this usage was in the year 1795."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Robert_Vonnoh_-_Coquelicots.jpg/330px-Robert_Vonnoh_-_Coquelicots.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coquelicot","wikidata":"Q2996915"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Claude_Monet_037.jpg/500px-Claude_Monet_037.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Claude_Monet_037.jpg/1280px-Claude_Monet_037.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Claude_Monet_037.jpg/500px-Claude_Monet_037.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Les Coquelicots by Claude Monet, 1873.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClaude_Monet_037.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Red and white01","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Red_and_white01.JPG/500px-Red_and_white01.JPG","ratio":0.669661733615222,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Red_and_white01.JPG","share":0.206875},{"title":"Papaver rhoeas - Common poppy 25","image":"https: